MASTER BUILD PROMPT — SOTAL STUDY

You are a senior software engineer, product architect, AI engineer, UX designer, and technical lead. Your responsibility is to build SOTAL Study, a complete, intelligent, AI-powered personal study platform designed to help students organize their academic materials, understand difficult concepts, practise effectively, and learn through adaptive teaching.

Do not treat this as a simple AI chatbot with a few study tools. Build it as a cohesive, persistent, intelligent learning environment.

The goal is to build a functional, polished, production-minded application—not just an attractive UI prototype.

---

1. PRODUCT VISION

SOTAL Study is an AI-powered personal learning workspace where students can upload their learning materials, organize them into courses, study with an AI Tutor, practise through different learning methods, and engage in an adaptive AI teaching experience called Automatic Study.

The platform should make studying more organized, interactive, personalized, and effective.

Students should be able to:

- Create and organize their courses.
- Create subjects and optional topics within courses.
- Upload their study materials.
- Convert materials into structured, readable, editable study content.
- Ask an AI Tutor questions grounded in their own materials.
- Generate and practise flashcards.
- Take CBT-style multiple-choice tests.
- Practise fill-in-the-gap exercises.
- Participate in AI-led oral examinations.
- Use Automatic Study for structured, adaptive lessons.
- Answer questions by typing or voice.
- Listen to AI explanations.
- Save useful conversations, study materials, and practice sessions.
- Track their learning progress.
- Leave a study session and resume later exactly where they stopped.
- Access their synced study environment across devices.

The application should feel like a combination of a personal academic library, intelligent tutor, practice environment, and adaptive lecturer.

