7.2 CBT — MULTIPLE-CHOICE TESTS

Generate structured CBT questions based on the selected materials.

Each question should normally contain four answer options.

Quality requirements

- One clearly correct answer by default.
- Plausible distractors.
- No ambiguous questions.
- No duplicated questions.
- No misleading wording.
- No answer leakage.
- No meaningless filler.
- Appropriate difficulty.
- Material-grounded questions.

CBT modes

Practice Mode

- Student answers a question.
- Feedback can appear immediately.
- Explain why the answer is correct or incorrect.
- Allow the student to continue.

Exam Mode

- Student answers without immediate feedback.
- Navigate between questions.
- Change answers.
- Flag questions.
- Track unanswered questions.
- Submit the test at the end.

CBT results

Show:

- Total score.
- Percentage.
- Correct answers.
- Incorrect answers.
- Questions skipped.
- Explanations.
- Weak topics.
- Areas needing improvement.

Allow:

- Retry.
- Retry missed questions.
- Review all questions.
- Save the test.
- Revisit previous results.

