14. FIREBASE AND CLOUD SYNCHRONIZATION

Use Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore.

Cloud data should synchronize across devices.

The Library should be cloud-synced by default. Do not make the core product local-only.

Firestore is the cloud source of truth

Persist:

- Courses.
- Topics.
- Study sources.
- Extracted content.
- Tutor conversations.
- Messages.
- Saved AI responses.
- Generated study materials.
- Study sessions.
- Session segments.
- Checkpoints.
- Study history.
- Preferences.

Suggested data structure

Use a user-scoped structure such as:

users/{userId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/topics/{topicId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/sources/{sourceId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/conversations/{conversationId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/conversations/{conversationId}/messages/{messageId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/studyMaterials/{materialId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/studySessions/{sessionId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/studySessions/{sessionId}/segments/{segmentId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/studySessions/{sessionId}/checkpoints/{checkpointId}

users/{userId}/courses/{courseId}/studyHistory/{historyId}

Refine this structure where necessary based on scalability, indexing, data size, and security requirements.

Local storage

Use IndexedDB for:

- Local caching.
- Offline-readable content.
- Drafts.
- Unsaved edits.
- Temporary document extraction.
- Temporary processing state.
- Recovery of interrupted workflows.

Local storage complements Firestore; it does not replace cloud synchronization.

Synchronization

Implement:

- Initial cloud loading.
- Local caching.
- Cloud updates.
- Create/update/delete synchronization.
- Offline handling.
- Recovery.
- Conflict handling where appropriate.
- Loading states.
- Error states.
- Retry mechanisms.

Do not create a fragile synchronization system that silently loses data.

Firestore security

Implement proper Firebase security rules.

Users must only access their own data.

Security must be enforced at the Firebase security-rule level, not merely by filtering data in frontend components.

Validate user ownership and access to nested records.

