19. DEVELOPMENT RULES

Follow these rules throughout development:

1. Inspect existing files before changing them.
2. Reuse working code where appropriate.
3. Do not unnecessarily rewrite the entire application.
4. Do not build fake buttons.
5. Do not create placeholder functionality and claim it is complete.
6. Do not silently discard user data.
7. Do not store API keys in cloud databases.
8. Do not expose user data across accounts.
9. Do not rely exclusively on chat transcripts for study-session continuation.
10. Do not generate low-quality learning questions.
11. Do not overload the student with excessively long lessons.
12. Do not implement Automatic Study as an ordinary chat conversation.
13. Do not fake progress metrics.
14. Do not pretend AI features work offline.
15. Do not begin the next phase while the current phase has unresolved foundational issues.
16. Keep architecture modular and maintainable.
17. Validate AI outputs.
18. Test real workflows.
19. Be honest about what is implemented and what remains unfinished.
20. Prioritize correctness, functionality, user experience, and reliable persistence over visual appearance alone.

