20. DEFINITION OF SUCCESS

SOTAL Study is successful when a student can complete the following end-to-end workflow without broken functionality:

1. Sign up or sign in.
2. Create a course.
3. Create topics if desired.
4. Upload a PDF, presentation, image, or handwritten note.
5. Extract and review its content.
6. Correct the content.
7. Save it to the cloud.
8. Open it later.
9. Ask the AI Tutor questions based on the source.
10. Receive useful, grounded explanations.
11. Save a conversation.
12. Generate flashcards.
13. Complete and review flashcards.
14. Generate and complete a CBT.
15. Review mistakes and explanations.
16. Complete a fill-in-the-gap exercise.
17. Participate in an AI oral examination.
18. Start Automatic Study.
19. Learn progressively through structured lessons.
20. Answer questions using text or voice.
21. Receive evaluation and scores.
22. Experience adaptive teaching when struggling.
23. Pause and leave a session.
24. Return later and resume exactly where they stopped.
25. Continue across conversation segments when necessary without repeating lessons.
26. View study history.
27. Reopen saved study materials.
28. Use voice playback.
29. Install the PWA.
30. Access synced data across devices.

The application must be genuinely functional, persistent, responsive, reliable, and designed for real students.

